# DROP A WHOLE STATIC 3D PACK IN HERE (props, buildings, vehicles, scenery —
# anything that is not an animated character; those go in ../characters/).
#
# Why this exists rather than dropping straight into ../../packs/: THAT folder's
# .gitignore keeps only .glb .gltf .bin .obj .mtl and silently discards
# everything else, textures included. An .obj or .gltf without its .png is a
# model that loads as a blank grey shape, and the loss is silent — git simply
# never mentions the files it ignored. This folder keeps the textures too, so
# the ingest can pack them into the .glb before anything reaches packs/.
#
# Everything here is excluded from the Vercel deploy by .vercelignore, so size
# here costs git history, never page load.

# ignore everything...
*

# ...but descend into directories so nested models are still found
!*/

# ...and keep the model formats the ingest reads
!*.glb
!*.gltf
!*.bin
!*.obj
!*.mtl

# textures a .gltf/.obj references by filename — WITHOUT THESE THE MODEL IS BLANK
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg

# licences are small and belong with the assets they cover
!LICENSE*
!License*
!license*
!*.txt

!README.md
!.gitignore
